 "C0": {
  "code": "INELIG",
  "loc": "Abstract, p. 1593; Section 4, p. 1595",
  "quote": "aggregate the queries using methods from social choice theory",
  "note": "The main object is rank aggregation of repeated LLM outputs to make query answering more robust, which is the codebook's 'ML rank aggregation' exclusion. The 'voters' are repeated prompts to one LLM, not several agents taking part in a collective decision. The paper borrows the Partial Borda Choice function and its known characterisation, but its contribution is the LLM robustness method and its empirical evaluation. Coding stopped."
